  <section class="brand-faq" aria-labelledby="merinoFaqTitle">
    <div class="container-lg">
      <div class="brand-faq__layout">
        <div class="brand-faq__intro">
          <p class="txt-light">(Merino Laminates)</p>
          <h2 id="merinoFaqTitle">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <p>Find quick answers to help you choose the right laminate surface for your space.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="brand-faq__list">
          <details open>
            <summary>What are laminates?</summary>
            <p>Laminates are durable decorative surface sheets made by bonding layers of paper and resin under heat and pressure.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Where can Merino laminates be used?</summary>
            <p>They are suitable for furniture, cabinets, wardrobes, doors, wall panels, countertops, and other interior surfaces.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are Merino laminates easy to maintain?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Wipe surfaces with a soft cloth and mild cleaner; avoid harsh chemicals and abrasive tools.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are laminates suitable for kitchens and bathrooms?</summary>
            <p>Choose the appropriate moisture- and heat-resistant laminate grade for kitchens, bathrooms, and other high-use areas.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How do I choose the right laminate?</summary>
            <p>Consider the intended application, required performance, finish, colour, texture, and the overall style of your space.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What types of laminates are available?</summary>
            <p>Merino offers decorative, high-pressure, metallic, digital, matte, gloss, textured, and performance laminate options.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are Merino laminates suitable for commercial spaces?</summary>
            <p>Yes. Their durable, easy-to-maintain surfaces are suitable for retail, office, hospitality, healthcare, and other commercial interiors.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Which finishes and textures are available?</summary>
            <p>Choose from a wide range of matte, high-gloss, woodgrain, solid, stone, patterned, and textured finishes.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is there a difference between laminates and mica?</summary>
            <p>Mica is the commonly used Indian name for decorative laminate sheets; both refer to layered surfacing materials used for interior finishes.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Do Merino laminates come with a warranty?</summary>
            <p>Merino provides a manufacturer warranty for eligible products. Please refer to the applicable warranty terms for your selected laminate.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
